  "claims": [
    "public mutate stages authored and managed source, membership, route, potential and reservation changes in one atomic transaction",
    "incremental route and potential-index traversal without tenant-wide source or producer scans in the writer",
    "final-graph causal closure including zero-output roles, changed bounds and cycles through unchanged downstream producers",
    "all old outputs of the pending cohort withdrawn before evaluation; unresolved contributions never treated as zero",
    "final typed references, unique claims and live potential empty-scope validators checked before one publication",
    "first-potential model and creation-time reservations retained through absence and retirement",
    "independent complete active source-derived inventories and structure checks cover business and private routing/potential state",
    "no-op mutations write nothing and disjoint producer changes do not trigger unrelated evaluations",
    "explicit logical budgets, atomic rollback and deliberately omitted-invalidation detection"
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "memory adapter remains serialized and volatile; no crash, durable receipt, distributed concurrency or production acceptance",
    "memory prefix scans enumerate the store; logical route/potential budgets do not bound physical scans, callbacks, bytes or all CPU work",
    "conservative interval reporting remains worst-case O(R); cascades, outputs and graph edges add work beyond AVL paths",
    "callbacks are trusted ordinary JavaScript, with required purity rather than a sandbox",
    "independent current-state checking cannot infer completeness of a missing retired historical reservation",
    "managed template model and creation time bind at first potential declaration and cannot be changed on reactivation",
    "JS-P4 bounded authorized readers/cursors and JS-P5 lifecycle/devtools remain unaccepted",
    "no Rust/legacy runtime suites rerun for this isolated Node checkpoint"
  ],
